## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/extrapolateboundaries.html
- Summary (EN): Extrapolate Boundaries fills empty areas of an image by copying colors outward from the edges of non-empty regions. It is typically used to add a bleed around texture maps so that mip-mapping does not pull black values into sampled areas.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Extrapolate Boundaries prolonge vers l'extérieur les couleurs des bords d'une zone, notamment pour ajouter un débord aux textures.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: Mono, UV, RGB or RGBA layer to extrapolate", "fillarea: layer defining the interior, which is extrapolated into the exterior", "mask: optional per-pixel mask amount scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Exterior: Unchanged, Black, or Diffuse Fill (smooth fill) for pixels beyond the edge padding", "Inner Side: Below Threshold or Above Threshold, which side of fillarea counts as inside", "Threshold: value separating inside from outside in fillarea; a dropper can set it from the layer", "Edge Padding: distance in image coordinates over which pixel values are copied directly outward", "Edge Offset: how far to backtrack when reading clean source values, so extrapolated exterior colors are not reused", "Sample Only Present: uses original values only from the source area, preventing black leaking from uninitialized areas", "Diffuse Iterations: relaxation passes smoothing the extrapolated values in Diffuse Fill mode"]

- Caveats: ["If the source is RGBA, consider splitting alpha with an RGBA to RGB node first, since alpha often defines the fillarea and RGB is the source", "With Sample Only Present on, Edge Offset can usually be set to 0; turning Sample Only Present off gives a smooth interpolated edge when the fillarea holds valid data"]

